    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0126" n="44" xml:id="pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860f.51/435: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-14T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1925—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 14—3
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Your 43, my 50. Commercial attaché reports that Zell of New York Trust
                    Company made positive statement to him that credit of $12,000,000 had actually
                    been made to Czechoslovak Banking Office. This statement was made by Zell
                    because of his interest in trying to ascertain if Federal Reserve Bank had made
                    similar credit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Einstein</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
